      "is_group": false,
      "description": "Business meaning: The raw, human-readable wait duration supplied by the batch operator or job scheduler at runtime via SYSIN, expressed as a character string of up to 8 digits representing centiseconds. This makes the delay fully configurable without requiring code changes, allowing operations teams to tune the timing interval between dependent batch jobs (e.g., specifying '00000500' for a 5-second pause) simply by adjusting the job stream input."
    }
